1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,300
Doctors have a strength test that predicts how long you'll live. It's not your bench. It's your grip.

2
00:00:06,550 --> 00:00:17,250
In a study of nearly 140,000 adults in 17 countries, every 5 kilos of grip lost meant 16 percent higher risk of death. A stronger signal than blood pressure.

3
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:26,750
Grip isn't a hand muscle. It's flexors that start at your elbow, run down the forearm, and become tendons that pull your fingers shut.

4
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:29,500
Here is the fix.

5
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:39,450
Three moves. Dead hangs, three sets of thirty seconds. Heavy farmer carries, three trips of forty metres. Plate pinches, twenty seconds at eight out of ten.

6
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:47,450
Can't hang thirty seconds yet? Keep your toes on a box, and build up to three sets of thirty.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,750
So test yourself: hang as long as you can, and comment your time.
